{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '380,510p' acceptance/check.mjs && sed -n '355,398p' docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md && sed -n '165,199p' docs/02-product-spec.md\"","aggregated_output":" * has no engine in its sidecar predates the switch (or holds Node tests): null.\n */\nfunction runEngine(file, results, provenance) {\n  const { engines, versions } = declaredEngines(results);\n  if (engines.length > 1) throw new Error(`${file}: mixes engines (${engines.join(', ')}); run each engine into its own results file`);\n  if (versions.length > 1) throw new Error(`${file}: mixes engine versions (${versions.join(', ')})`);\n  const recorded = provenance?.engine;\n  if (recorded !== undefined && recorded !== null && !ENGINES.includes(recorded)) throw new Error(`${file}: unknown engine in provenance: ${recorded}`);\n  if (engines.length && recorded && recorded !== engines[0]) {\n    throw new Error(`${file}: the provenance records ${recorded} but the results declare ${engines[0]}`);\n  }\n  const engine = engines[0] ?? recorded ?? null;\n  return { engine, engineVersion: versions.length ? versions[0].slice(engine.length + 1) : provenance?.engineVersion ?? null };\n}\n\n/**\n * The engine one test ran on. Its own record when it has one. Without one, Chrome only in a run that is\n * Chrome or predates the switch: every browser launcher in this repository that does not read AXYLO_ENGINE\n * (apps/docs/test, tests/dist/browser.ts) launches system Chrome. In a run on another engine such a test is\n * \"engine not recorded\" (null) and stands for no engine.\n */\nfunction testEngine(test, runEngine) {\n  if (test.meta?.engine !== undefined) return test.meta.engine;\n  return runEngine === null || runEngine === 'chromium' ? 'chromium' : null;\n}\n\nconst testKey = (ancestors, title) => JSON.stringify([ancestors, title]);\nconst inSuite = (ancestors, prefix) => ancestors.some(suite => suite !== null && suite.startsWith(prefix));\n\n/** Whether a test the scan found (ancestors with null for a suite of unknown title) is this reported one. */\nconst sameTest = (known, reported) => known.title === reported.title && known.ancestors.length === reported.ancestorTitles.length\n  && known.ancestors.every((suite, i) => suite === null || suite === reported.ancestorTitles[i]);\n\nfunction resultFor(source, ref, context) {\n  const { results, suiteFailures, stale, pack, sizeTargets } = context;\n  const reasons = new Set();\n  if (ref.kind === 'size') {\n    // A size record counts only for the pack it measured, and that pack must be the one this tree packs.\n    if (source.size.integrity !== pack()) {\n      reasons.add(`${basename(source.path)}: the size record measured another pack (${source.size.integrity.slice(0, 19)}…), not the one this tree packs (${String(pack()).slice(0, 19)}…)`);\n      return { status: STALE, reports: new Map([[source.path, new Set(['not recorded'])]]), reasons };\n    }\n    const exceeded = ref.entries.some(name => exceeds(source.size.rows.get(name).totalGzipBytes, sizeTargets[name]));\n    const status = exceeded ? 'fail' : 'pass';\n    return { status, reports: new Map([[source.path, new Set([status])]]), reasons };\n  }\n  const reports = new Map();\n  if (!testKinds.includes(ref.kind)) return { status: 'not run', reports, reasons };\n  // A browser citation is answered only by results of its own engine: a pass elsewhere is no evidence here.\n  const engine = ref.kind === 'browser' ? ref.engine ?? 'chromium' : null;\n  const sameEngine = test => engine === null || test.engine === engine;\n  const known = ref.ancestors ? [{ title: ref.title, ancestors: ref.ancestors }] : ref.registration\n    ? source.titles.templates.filter(test => test.template === ref.registration).map(test => ({ title: ref.title, ancestors: test.ancestors }))\n    : source.titles.tests.filter(({ title, ancestors }) => ref.title\n      ? title === ref.title : inSuite(ancestors, ref.prefix) && (!ref.casePrefix || title?.startsWith(ref.casePrefix)));\n  // Under atLeast, the cases the scan could not list are counted from the results instead.\n  const expected = ref.atLeast ? known.filter(test => test.title !== null) : known;\n  const templates = ref.casePrefix ? source.titles.templates.filter(test => inSuite(test.ancestors, ref.prefix)) : [];\n  for (const [file, runEngine] of suiteFailures.get(source.path) ?? []) {\n    if (!(engine === null || runEngine === engine || (runEngine === null && engine === 'chromium'))) continue;\n    if (stale.has(file)) {\n      reports.set(file, new Set(['not recorded']));\n      reasons.add(`${basename(file)}: not recorded for this revision (${stale.get(file)})`);\n    } else reports.set(file, new Set(['fail']));\n  }\n  const passed = [];\n  for (const test of results.get(source.path) ?? []) {\n    const matches = ref.prefix ? inSuite(test.ancestorTitles, ref.prefix) && (!ref.casePrefix || test.title.startsWith(ref.casePrefix))\n      : ref.ancestors ? known.some(k => sameTest(k, test)) : test.title === ref.title;\n    if (!matches) continue;\n    if (!sameEngine(test)) {\n      if (test.engine === null) reasons.add(`${basename(test.file)}: engine not recorded in a ${engineLabel(test.runEngine)} run`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    // A run whose provenance does not match this tree answers nothing about it.\n    if (stale.has(test.file)) {\n      if (!reports.has(test.file)) reports.set(test.file, new Set());\n      reports.get(test.file).add('not recorded');\n      reasons.add(`${basename(test.file)}: not recorded for this revision (${stale.get(test.file)})`);\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (test.status !== 'passed' && test.status !== 'failed' && isText(test.meta?.notRun)) reasons.add(`Not run on ${test.meta.notRun}`);\n    // Historical failures remain visible even when a suite has since replaced the assertion.\n    if (test.status === 'passed' && (!ref.casePrefix || expected.some(k => sameTest(k, test))\n      || templates.some(candidate => sameTest({ title: test.title, ancestors: candidate.ancestors }, test) && matchesTemplate(test.title, candidate.template)))) {\n      passed.push(test);\n    }\n    if (!reports.has(test.file)) reports.set(test.file, new Set());\n    reports.get(test.file).add(test.status === 'failed' ? 'fail' : test.status === 'passed' ? 'pass' : 'skipped');\n  }\n  const distinct = new Set(passed.map(test => testKey(test.ancestorTitles, test.title))).size;\n  const current = [...reports.values()].filter(values => !values.has('not recorded'));\n  const status = current.some(values => values.has('fail')) ? 'fail'\n    : distinct && (!ref.cases || distinct === ref.cases) && (!ref.atLeast || distinct >= ref.atLeast)\n      && expected.every(k => passed.some(test => sameTest(k, test))) && current.every(values => !values.has('skipped')) ? 'pass'\n      : [...reports.values()].some(values => values.has('not recorded')) ? STALE : 'not run';\n  if (status === 'not run') {\n    const citation = `${ref.file}: ${ref.title ?? ref.prefix}${ref.casePrefix ? ` (${ref.casePrefix})` : ''}`;\n    if (ref.atLeast && distinct < ref.atLeast && current.length) {\n      reasons.add(`${distinct} of at least ${ref.atLeast} cases passed for ${citation}`);\n    } else if ((current.length || !reasons.size) && current.every(values => !values.has('skipped'))) {\n      if (engine !== null && !reports.size) reasons.add(`No ${engineLabel(engine)} result for ${citation}`);\n      else if (ref.cases && distinct && distinct !== ref.cases) reasons.add(`Expected ${ref.cases} passing cases for ${citation}, found ${distinct}`);\n      else reasons.add(`No matching passing test for ${citation}`);\n    }\n  }\n  return { status, reports, reasons };\n}\n\nfunction cellFor(row, type, root, sources, context) {\n  if (!row.appliesTo.includes(type)) return { status: 'not applicable', reports: new Map(), unrun: [], reasons: new Set() };\n  const required = row.evidence?.[type] ?? [];\n  const weak = row.weak?.[type] ?? [];\n  const outcome = ref => resultFor(sources.get(resolve(root, ref.file)), ref, context);\n  const outcomes = required.map(outcome);\n  const supporting = weak.map(outcome);\n  let status;\n  if ([...outcomes, ...supporting].some(result => result.status === 'fail')) status = 'fail';\n  else if (row.cannotVerify?.[type]) status = 'cannot be verified here';\n  else if (row.pending?.[type]) status = 'not run';\n  else if (row.gaps?.[type] || (!required.length && weak.length)) status = 'weak';\n  else if (!required.length) status = 'no evidence';\n  else if ([...outcomes, ...supporting].every(result => result.status === 'pass')) status = 'pass';\n  else status = [...outcomes, ...supporting].some(result => result.status === STALE) ? STALE : 'not run';\n\n  const reports = new Map();\n  for (const { reports: matches } of [...outcomes, ...supporting]) for (const [file, values] of matches) {\n    if (!reports.has(file)) reports.set(file, new Set());\n    for (const value of values) reports.get(file).add(value);\n  }\n  const unrun = [...required.filter((ref, i) => testKinds.includes(ref.kind) && outcomes[i].status === 'not run'),\n- The packed tarball installed into two clean fixtures (npm with a bundler, script tag): the first chart works in ten lines or fewer in each (DX1).\n- Node import and `validate()` without a DOM; strict CSP with real headers (DX8).\n- Size measured on the packed distribution for line-only, full and script-tag cases, CSS included (DX7).\n- Every runnable docs example compiled and rendered from the packed distribution (DX10).\n- The agent rehearsal (DX12), recorded as rehearsal.\n\n### M8. Release (ceiling: 10 days)\n\n- Beta under a `next` tag; issues from real use fixed; API frozen through the API report.\n- The Phase 1 comparison regenerated with Axylo beside the ten libraries, with the same harness and the corrections from the review, and published with its limits.\n- Real Safari on macOS and iOS checked by hand.\n- Independent review of the acceptance evidence before 1.0 is tagged, by a reviewer who did not write the code under review.\n\nOutcomes: every acceptance-matrix row is pass or not applicable with a reason; changelog, upgrade policy and third-party notices published.\n\nPublishing to npm, tagging and pushing are separate, explicit decisions by the owner at this point; the plan does not assume them.\n\n## 4. Test strategy\n\n| Layer | Tool | What it proves |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unit | Vitest | Scales, ticks, formatting, parsing, simplification. |\n| Property | fast-check | Invariants that must hold for any data: F1, F2, F5, F7, F11, L1. |\n| Scene snapshot | Vitest, injected text metrics | Geometry and text for each fixture and width, without a browser. |\n| Browser | Playwright on three engines | Real text boxes, resize, pointer, touch, keyboard, time zones, color schemes, reduced motion, fonts loading late. |\n| Accessibility | axe-core, accessibility-tree snapshots, keyboard scripts, recorded rehearsal | A1–A10. |\n| Visual | Screenshots per operating system | What the scene cannot see: antialiasing, state leaks. |\n| Types | `docs/api/examples.ts` pattern | The listed mistakes fail to compile (DX3). |\n| Packed distribution | Clean install fixtures | What users actually get (DX1, DX7, DX8, DX10). |\n| Acceptance matrix | Data file plus a checker | Every criterion has a test that exists and a current result; stale criterion IDs fail CI. |\n\nExpected values are derived from the spec and the fixture data, never from the implementation's output. A failing test is fixed in the code or escalated as a spec question, never by editing the expected value to match.\n\n## 5. Risks\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| The interaction pattern that works in one screen reader fails in another. | Three candidates rehearsed on five pairs in M1, before any of the surrounding DOM is built. Plot roles are internal and can change in a minor release. |\n| DOM text costs too much with many charts on a page. | P5 is measured in M1. A fallback to canvas-drawn tick labels would give up user text spacing and forced-colors adaptation for those labels, so it must pass the same L1 and A6 tests before it is allowed. |\n| Size targets and features conflict. | Measured from M1; each milestone records its byte cost. Accessibility is not what gets cut; chart types are. |\n| The million-point budget cannot be met with exact lookup and gap-preserving simplification. | The headline claim is already limited to measured workloads (spec, section 1). If P2 fails after tuning, the budget is changed in the spec with the measurements, not hidden. |\n| Layout promises collide in small tiles. | L8 defines the fallback; the property test covers down to 240 px. |\n| One person cannot hand-check real Safari, iOS, Android and Windows screen readers at every milestone. | Automated checks at every milestone; the manual rehearsal at M1, M4 and M8 only, recorded with dates and versions. Device access is a named dependency of those three milestones. |\n| Scope growth through chart-type requests. | Section 6. |\n| AX110 | Warning | An author domain on bar or area excluded zero | Domain widened to zero |\n| AX111 | Hint | Instants look like calendar dates | As instants, zone shown |\n| AX112 | Hint | Date-time strings have no offset | As written |\n| AX120 | Error | Negative donut value | Error state |\n| AX121 | Warning | More than eight donut slices | Seven largest plus \"Other (n)\" |\n| AX130 | Warning | More than eight series | All series, with dash or marker differences |\n| AX140 | Warning | No `title` and no `labelledBy` | Generated name |\n| AX141 | Warning | Palette below 3:1 on the resolved background | As themed |\n| AX142 | Hint | Plot too small to draw | Summary and table control |\n| AX143 | Hint | Labels hidden after every remedy | Note shown to the reader |\n| AX150 | Warning | Unknown option key | Ignored; the message suggests the closest known key |\n| AX151 | Warning | `append` rows out of order | Accepted through the slower full update |\n| AX131 | Hint | A compact chart has more than one series | Drawn, with dash differences |\n| AX132 | Hint | More bars than pixels along the category axis | Drawn; the message suggests aggregating |\n| AX133 | Hint | A scatter chart has more than 50,000 points | Drawn; the message says drawing may be slow |\n| AX134 | Error | Series × x positions exceeds 20,000,000 (long rows with many series and little shared x) | Error state; the message gives both counts and suggests fewer series or a scatter chart |\n| AX152 | Warning | `timeZone` is not a zone the browser knows | The viewer's zone is used |\n| AX160 | Warning | A custom formatter threw | The default format is used for that value. A value formatter that throws changes how a value reads, so the reader's note (F12) is shown; a tick formatter that throws only changes an axis label, which is not a value left out or changed, so it is reported without a note (and so the note can never change which ticks fit) |\n| AX199 | Error | An error was thrown while Axylo was building the chart: by Axylo itself, or by code the author supplied that Axylo was running (a row getter, a callback; a formatter that throws is AX160, and the default format is used) | Error state with a generic message; the error is passed to `onDiagnostic` and printed |\n\nExpected results for the Phase 1 fixtures: the combined `dirty` fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`) yields AX102, AX103 and AX106 once each, draws Mon–Tue as a segment and Sun as a point, and shows the F12 note. `dirty-string` (one `'40'` among numbers) yields AX106. A column made only of numeric strings yields AX104 and is drawn in full. `dirty-null` yields nothing.\n\nThe split between AX104 and AX106 answers a reviewer's objection that common back ends return counts as strings (Postgres `bigint` and `numeric`, BigQuery): a whole column of plain decimal strings is unambiguous and is parsed; a stray string among numbers is a bug and is not.\n\n### 3.6 Type matrix\n\n| | Line | Area | Bar | Donut | Scatter |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Picking by pointer | Nearest x | Nearest x | The band under the pointer | The slice under the pointer | Nearest point within 24 px; ties go to the later row |\n| Tooltip content | Every visible series at that x | Same, plus the stack total | Every series in that category | Label, value, percentage | The point's series, x and y; coincident points listed, up to eight |\n| Keyboard order | By x, then series | By x, then series | By category, then series | By slice order | By x, then y |\n| Zoom | On time, date and numeric x only | On time, date and numeric x only | On time, date and numeric x only | No | Yes, both axes later; x only in 1.0 |\n| Simplified drawing when dense | F5 | F5 on cumulative sums | No; more bars than pixels raises a hint | No | No in 1.0; above 50,000 points a hint says drawing may be slow |\n| Limit that raises a diagnostic | Eight series | Eight series | Eight series | Eight slices | Eight series |\n| Reference lines and bands | Yes; included in the domain; listed in the summary and table caption | Yes | Yes | No | Yes |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
