{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat apps/docs/lib/conformance.mjs && cat apps/docs/test/conformance.test.ts && cat apps/docs/pages/conformance.md'","aggregated_output":"/**\n * The data of the conformance page (spec A9), read when the site is built, so the page cannot say more than\n * its sources do:\n *\n * - which WCAG 2.2 success criteria the specification cites, and in which of its criterion rows\n *   (docs/02-product-spec.md; a row cites \"WCAG 2.5.1, 2.5.7\" in its last column, spec A9);\n * - what the acceptance checker reports for those rows: `check()` of acceptance/check.mjs, in release mode,\n *   over the result files acceptance/run.mjs writes (acceptance/results/<config>[-<engine>].json, named by\n *   provenance.mjs), so a result counts only when its recorded provenance matches the working tree;\n * - which engine each result came from: the checker's record of each report, or for a result that predates\n *   the engine record, the engine its default result file runs on (provenance.mjs `resultFiles()`).\n *\n * Nothing here judges evidence: a criterion without a counted result is \"not recorded\", and when the checker\n * refuses its matrix nothing is counted at all. Checker output this module cannot read stops the build,\n * rather than being shown as something it is not.\n */\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { splitRow } from './markdown.mjs';\nimport { wcag } from '../data/wcag.mjs';\nimport { check, CHART_TYPES, STATUSES } from '../../../acceptance/check.mjs';\nimport { ENGINES, engineLabel, resultFiles as defaultResultFiles } from '../../../acceptance/provenance.mjs';\n\nconst SC = /\\d\\.\\d{1,2}\\.\\d{1,2}\\b/g;\n/**\n * What a report can say of the tests it answered: their results, or 'not recorded' when its provenance is\n * another tree or pack, which the checker gives only with a `provenanceError` (README, \"Reading the checker\").\n */\nconst RESULTS = ['pass', 'fail', 'skipped', 'not recorded'];\n\nconst bySc = (a, b) => {\n  const x = a.split('.').map(Number);\n  const y = b.split('.').map(Number);\n  return x[0] - y[0] || x[1] - y[1] || x[2] - y[2];\n};\n\n/**\n * Success criterion → the specification's rows that cite it, each with its criterion text (Markdown). A row\n * cites \"WCAG x.y.z\" in its last column (spec A9); a mention elsewhere in the row is not a citation.\n */\nexport function citedCriteria(spec) {\n  const cited = new Map();\n  for (const line of spec.split(/\\r?\\n/)) {\n    if (!line.startsWith('|')) continue;\n    const cells = splitRow(line);\n    const id = cells[0].replace(/[*_`]/g, '');\n    if (!/^[A-Z]+\\d+$/.test(id)) continue;\n    for (const cell of cells.slice(-1)) {\n      for (const m of cell.matchAll(/WCAG((?:[\\s,]+(?:and\\s+)?\\d\\.\\d{1,2}\\.\\d{1,2}\\b)+)/g)) {\n        for (const sc of m[1].match(SC)) {\n          if (!wcag[sc]) throw new Error(`docs/02-product-spec.md, ${id}: WCAG ${sc} is not a level A or AA criterion of WCAG 2.2 (apps/docs/data/wcag.mjs)`);\n          if (!cited.has(sc)) cited.set(sc, []);\n          if (!cited.get(sc).some(row => row.id === id)) cited.get(sc).push({ id, criterion: cells[1] });\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return new Map([...cited].sort(([a], [b]) => bySc(a, b)));\n}\n\nconst unreadable = what => { throw new Error(`acceptance checker: output this page cannot read: ${what}`); };\n\n/**\n * The checker's `rows` → row id → { statement, cells: { chartType: { status, reports } } }, each report with\n * the engine it ran on (`engineOf` names it for a report the checker could not: results older than the engine\n * record), whether it counts for this revision, and the commit it was recorded at. Anything outside the\n * checker's documented shape stops the build.\n */\nexport function readRows(rows, { engineOf = () => null, commitOf = () => null } = {}) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(rows)) unreadable('rows is not a list');\n  const out = new Map();\n  for (const row of rows) {\n    if (typeof row?.id !== 'string' || typeof row.statement !== 'string' || row.cells === null || typeof row.cells !== 'object') unreadable(JSON.stringify(row)?.slice(0, 80));\n    const types = Object.keys(row.cells);\n    if (types.length !== CHART_TYPES.length || types.some((type, i) => type !== CHART_TYPES[i])) unreadable(`${row.id}: chart types ${types.join(', ')}`);\n    const cells = {};\n    for (const type of types) {\n      const cell = row.cells[type];\n      if (!STATUSES.includes(cell?.status) || !Array.isArray(cell.reports)) unreadable(`${row.id}/${type}: status ${cell?.status}`);\n      cells[type] = {\n        status: cell.status,\n        reports: cell.reports.map(report => {\n          if (typeof report?.file !== 'string' || !['run', 'size'].includes(report.source) || !Array.isArray(report.results)\n            || report.results.some(r => !RESULTS.includes(r)) || !(report.engine === null || ENGINES.includes(report.engine))\n            || !(report.provenanceError === null || typeof report.provenanceError === 'string')\n            || (report.results.includes('not recorded') && report.provenanceError === null)) {\n            unreadable(`${row.id}/${type}: report ${JSON.stringify(report)?.slice(0, 160)}`);\n          }\n          return {\n            file: report.file, source: report.source, results: report.results,\n            engine: report.source === 'size' ? null : report.engine ?? engineOf(report.file),\n            counted: report.provenanceError === null, why: report.provenanceError, commit: commitOf(report.file),\n          };\n        }),\n      };\n    }\n    out.set(row.id, { statement: row.statement, cells });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nconst json = file => JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8'));\n\n/**\n * Runs the checker on `root` (the repository; a test passes the checker's own fixtures). Returns what it\n * reported, or its refusal: `refused` holds its error lines, and then no row has a status. `files` are the\n * result files given, with what their sidecars record. By default the result files are acceptance/run.mjs's\n * default ones that exist under `root`.\n */\nexport async function readChecker({ root, matrixFile = path.join(root, 'acceptance/matrix.json'), resultFiles, packIntegrity, sizeTargets } = {}) {\n  const defaults = defaultResultFiles();\n  const engineOf = file => defaults.find(d => d.file === file)?.engine ?? null;\n  const given = resultFiles ?? defaults.map(d => path.join(root, d.file));\n  const present = given.filter(file => fs.existsSync(file)).map(file => path.relative(root, file).split(path.sep).join('/'));\n  const files = present.map(file => {\n    const sidecar = path.join(root, file.replace(/\\.json$/, '.provenance.json'));\n    const provenance = fs.existsSync(sidecar) ? json(sidecar) : null;\n    return { file, provenance, engine: provenance?.engine ?? engineOf(file) };\n  });\n  const label = engine => engine === null ? 'Node' : engineLabel(engine);\n  let result;\n  try {\n    // The checker packs the tree once (npm pack --dry-run) when the matrix cites a size record; a test names the\n    // pack and the targets itself (check()'s `packIntegrity` and `sizeTargets`).\n    const extra = { ...(packIntegrity === undefined ? {} : { packIntegrity }), ...(sizeTargets === undefined ? {} : { sizeTargets }) };\n    result = check({ root, matrixFile, resultFiles: present.map(file => path.join(root, file)), release: true, ...extra });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { refused: String(error.message).split('\\n').filter(Boolean), rows: new Map(), citations: new Map(), files, label, warnings: [] };\n  }\n  const commitOf = file => files.find(f => f.file === file)?.provenance?.commit ?? null;\n  const rows = readRows(result.rows, { engineOf, commitOf });\n  if (!Array.isArray(result.warnings) || result.warnings.some(w => typeof w !== 'string')) unreadable('warnings is not a list of text');\n  for (const run of result.runs) {\n    const file = path.relative(root, run.file).split(path.sep).join('/');\n    const known = files.find(f => f.file === file);\n    if (known) Object.assign(known, { engine: run.engine ?? known.engine, counted: !run.provenanceError, why: run.provenanceError ?? null });\n  }\n  // The tests each row cites, once the checker has accepted the matrix (so every citation names a real test).\n  const citations = new Map();\n  for (const row of json(matrixFile)) {\n    const seen = new Map();\n    for (const refs of Object.values(row.evidence ?? {})) for (const ref of refs) {\n      const test = ref.title ?? (ref.prefix ? `${ref.prefix}…${ref.atLeast ? ` (at least ${ref.atLeast} cases)` : ''}` : null);\n      const entry = { kind: ref.kind, file: ref.file, test, engine: ref.kind === 'browser' ? ref.engine ?? 'chromium' : null };\n      seen.set(JSON.stringify(entry), entry);\n    }\n    citations.set(row.id, [...seen.values()]);\n  }\n  return { refused: null, rows, citations, files, label, warnings: result.warnings };\n}\n\n/**\n * For one criterion: the checker's verdict over the specification rows that cite it, and what each engine's\n * results said, for this revision only. Every answer is the checker's or \"not recorded\".\n */\nexport function evidenceFor(rows, checker) {\n  const engines = ['chromium', 'firefox', 'webkit', null];\n  const empty = Object.fromEntries(engines.map(engine => [String(engine), 'not recorded']));\n  if (checker.refused) return { verdict: rows.map(row => ({ id: row.id, text: 'not recorded' })), engines: empty };\n  const verdict = [];\n  const seen = new Map(engines.map(engine => [String(engine), { results: new Set(), stale: new Set() }]));\n  for (const { id } of rows) {\n    const row = checker.rows.get(id);\n    if (!row) {\n      verdict.push({ id, text: 'not recorded' });\n      continue;\n    }\n    const groups = new Map();\n    let stale = false;\n    for (const [type, cell] of Object.entries(row.cells)) {\n      if (!groups.has(cell.status)) groups.set(cell.status, []);\n      groups.get(cell.status).push(type);\n      if (cell.status === 'not applicable') continue;\n      for (const report of cell.reports) {\n        if (!report.counted) stale = true;\n        // A size measurement is no engine's: it counts in the checker's verdict only.\n        if (report.source === 'size') continue;\n        const bucket = seen.get(String(report.engine));\n        if (report.counted) for (const value of report.results) bucket.results.add(value);\n        else bucket.stale.add(report.commit ? report.commit.slice(0, 7) : 'unknown');\n      }\n    }\n    verdict.push({\n      id,\n      text: stale ? 'not recorded for this revision' : [...groups].map(([status, types]) => `${status} (${types.join(', ')})`).join('; '),\n    });\n  }\n  const say = ({ results, stale }) => results.size ? [...results].sort().join('/')\n    : stale.size ? `not recorded for this revision (results from ${[...stale].join(', ')})` : 'not recorded';\n  return { verdict, engines: Object.fromEntries([...seen].map(([engine, bucket]) => [engine, say(bucket)])) };\n}\n\n/** The level A and AA criteria the specification does not cite. */\nexport function uncited(cited) {\n  return Object.keys(wcag).filter(sc => !cited.has(sc)).sort(bySc);\n}\n\nexport async function readConformance({ root }) {\n  const spec = fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, 'docs/02-product-spec.md'), 'utf8');\n  const cited = citedCriteria(spec);\n  const checker = await readChecker({ root });\n  const criteria = [...cited].map(([sc, rows]) => ({\n    sc, name: wcag[sc][0], level: wcag[sc][1], rows, ...evidenceFor(rows, checker),\n    tests: rows.flatMap(row => checker.citations.get(row.id) ?? []).filter((t, i, all) => all.findIndex(u => JSON.stringify(u) === JSON.stringify(t)) === i),\n  }));\n  return { criteria, checker, uncited: uncited(cited).map(sc => {\n    const [name, level, kind, why] = wcag[sc];\n    if (!kind || !why) throw new Error(`apps/docs/data/wcag.mjs: WCAG ${sc} is cited by no row of the specification and needs a reason (spec A9)`);\n    return { sc, name, level, kind, why };\n  }) };\n}\n/**\n * The conformance page's data (lib/conformance.mjs): it may say only what the specification and the\n * acceptance checker record.\n *\n * - The criteria come from the specification: every \"WCAG x.y.z\" in the last column of a criterion row (spec\n *   A9), and only those; every criterion no row cites has a reason in data/wcag.mjs.\n * - The checker's structured rows are read as its README documents them, and output outside that shape stops\n *   the build.\n * - Against the checker's own fixtures (acceptance/test/fixtures, whose expected cells its own tests state):\n *   a result without recorded provenance, and a size record of another pack, are \"not recorded for this\n *   revision\" (the checker's status, with 'not recorded' as the report's result), and a refused matrix\n *   leaves every criterion \"not recorded\".\n */\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { citedCriteria, evidenceFor, readChecker, readConformance, readRows, uncited } from '../lib/conformance.mjs';\nimport { wcag } from '../data/wcag.mjs';\nimport { cacheDir, repoRoot } from '../lib/examples.mjs';\nimport { stageSite } from '../lib/site.mjs';\nimport { check, CHART_TYPES } from '../../../acceptance/check.mjs';\nimport { citedTestFiles, defaultResultFile, hashFile, snapshot } from '../../../acceptance/provenance.mjs';\n\nconst fixtures = path.join(repoRoot, 'acceptance/test/fixtures');\nconst spec = fs.readFileSync(path.join(repoRoot, 'docs/02-product-spec.md'), 'utf8');\n\ndescribe('the criteria the specification cites', () => {\n  it('reads citations from the last column of a criterion row, and nothing else', () => {\n    const text = [\n      '| ID | Criterion | Verified by | Driven by |',\n      '|---|---|---|---|',\n      '| I3 | Zoom four ways. | Clicks only | D7, R12, WCAG 2.5.1, 2.5.7, 1.4.4 |',\n      '| L1 | Labels never overlap. | Repeated with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides | R2 |',\n      '| A9 | Lists every applicable WCAG 2.2 AA success criterion. | CI | R11 |',\n      '| Picking by pointer | WCAG 1.4.13 | x | x |',\n      'Prose that names WCAG 2.4.7 outside a table.',\n    ].join('\\n');\n    const cited = citedCriteria(text);\n    expect([...cited.keys()]).toEqual(['1.4.4', '2.5.1', '2.5.7']);\n    expect(cited.get('2.5.7')).toEqual([{ id: 'I3', criterion: 'Zoom four ways.' }]);\n  });\n\n  it('a criterion that is not level A or AA of WCAG 2.2 stops the build', () => {\n    expect(() => citedCriteria('| X1 | Something. | x | WCAG 1.4.6 |')).toThrow(/1\\.4\\.6/);\n  });\n\n  it('on the specification: every number a \"WCAG\" in a criterion row\\'s last column names is listed', () => {\n    const cited = citedCriteria(spec);\n    const named = new Set<string>();\n    for (const line of spec.split('\\n')) {\n      if (!/^\\| [A-Z]+\\d+ \\|/.test(line)) continue;\n      const last = line.replace(/\\|\\s*$/, '').split('|').at(-1)!;\n      for (const m of last.matchAll(/WCAG ((?:\\d\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(?:, )?)+)/g)) for (const n of m[1]!.split(', ')) named.add(n);\n    }\n    expect(named.size).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    expect([...cited.keys()].sort()).toEqual([...named].sort());\n  });\n\n  it('every criterion no row cites has a reason: one of the two A9 names, or \"not assessed\"', () => {\n    const kinds = ['not applicable to a chart component', 'the page\\'s responsibility', 'not assessed'];\n    const missing = uncited(citedCriteria(spec)).filter(sc => !kinds.includes(wcag[sc]![2]!) || !wcag[sc]![3]);\n    expect(missing).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('reading the checker', () => {\n  const fixtureRun = () => check({ root: fixtures, matrixFile: path.join(fixtures, 'matrix.json'), resultFiles: [path.join(fixtures, 'results.json')] });\n\n  it('reads the checker\\'s rows on its fixtures as its own tests state them', () => {\n    const rows = readRows(fixtureRun().rows);\n    const f1 = rows.get('F1')!.cells;\n    expect(Object.keys(f1)).toEqual(['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact']);\n    expect(f1.line).toEqual({ status: 'pass', reports: [{ file: 'results.json', source: 'run', results: ['pass'], engine: null, counted: true, why: null, commit: null }] });\n    expect(f1.area!.status).toBe('weak');\n    expect(f1.area!.reports.map(r => r.results)).toEqual([['skipped']]);\n    expect(f1.scatter).toEqual({ status: 'not applicable', reports: [] });\n    expect(rows.get('F2')!.cells.line!.status).toBe('cannot be verified here');\n  });\n\n  it('names the engine of a report that has none from its default result file', () => {\n    const rows = readRows(fixtureRun().rows, { engineOf: file => file === 'results.json' ? 'chromium' : null, commitOf: () => 'abc1234' });\n    expect(rows.get('F1')!.cells.line!.reports[0]).toMatchObject({ engine: 'chromium', commit: 'abc1234' });\n  });\n\n  it('stops on output outside the documented shape', () => {\n    const good = fixtureRun().rows;\n    const change = (edit: (row: Record<string, any>) => void) => {\n      const rows = structuredClone(good) as Record<string, any>[];\n      edit(rows[0]!);\n      return () => readRows(rows);\n    };\n    expect(change(row => { row.cells.line.status = 'passed'; })).toThrow(/cannot read/);\n    expect(change(row => { delete row.cells.compact; })).toThrow(/cannot read/);\n    expect(change(row => { row.cells.line.reports = [{ file: 'x.json', source: 'run', results: ['green'], engine: null, provenanceError: null }]; })).toThrow(/cannot read/);\n    expect(change(row => { row.cells.line.reports = [{ file: 'x.json', source: 'run', results: ['pass'], engine: 'safari', provenanceError: null }]; })).toThrow(/cannot read/);\n    expect(() => readRows(undefined)).toThrow(/cannot read/);\n    // 'not recorded' is a result only with the provenance error that explains it.\n    expect(change(row => { row.cells.line.reports = [{ file: 'x.json', source: 'run', results: ['not recorded'], engine: null, provenanceError: null }]; })).toThrow(/cannot read/);\n    expect(change(row => { row.cells.line.reports = [{ file: 'x.json', source: 'run', results: ['not recorded'], engine: null, provenanceError: 'provenance does not match the working tree' }]; })).not.toThrow();\n    expect(change(row => { row.cells.line.status = 'not recorded for this revision'; })).not.toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it('a result without recorded provenance is not counted for this revision', async () => {\n    const checker = await readChecker({ root: fixtures, matrixFile: path.join(fixtures, 'matrix.json'), resultFiles: [path.join(fixtures, 'results.json')] });\n    expect(checker.refused).toBeNull();\n    const { verdict, engines } = evidenceFor([{ id: 'F1', criterion: '' }], checker);\n    expect(verdict).toEqual([{ id: 'F1', text: 'not recorded for this revision' }]);\n    expect(engines.null).toBe('not recorded for this revision (results from unknown)');\n    expect(engines.chromium).toBe('not recorded');\n  });\n\n  it('the checker\\'s own \"not recorded for this revision\": a run without provenance in a release', async () => {\n    const checker = await readChecker({ root: fixtures, matrixFile: path.join(fixtures, 'matrix.json'), resultFiles: [path.join(fixtures, 'results.json')] });\n    const line = checker.rows.get('F1')!.cells.line!;\n    expect(line.status).toBe('not recorded for this revision');\n    expect(line.reports).toEqual([{ file: 'results.json', source: 'run', results: ['not recorded'], engine: null, counted: false, why: 'release requires recorded provenance', commit: null }]);\n    expect(checker.files).toEqual([expect.objectContaining({ file: 'results.json', counted: false, why: 'release requires recorded provenance' })]);\n  });\n\n  it('counts matching provenance while the docs build stages its output', async () => {\n    fs.mkdirSync(cacheDir, { recursive: true });\n    const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(cacheDir, 'conformance-'));\n    try {\n      const write = (relative: string, contents: string | Buffer) => {\n        const file = path.join(root, relative);\n        fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(file), { recursive: true });\n        fs.writeFileSync(file, contents);\n        return file;\n      };\n      write('.gitignore', fs.readFileSync(path.join(repoRoot, '.gitignore')));\n      const statement = 'Show the fixture faithfully.';\n      const citations = [...citedCriteria(spec).keys()].join(', ');\n      const specFile = write('docs/02-product-spec.md', `### 3.1 Faithful representation\\n| F1 | ${statement} | WCAG ${citations} |\\n`);\n      const file = 'chart.test.ts';\n      const title = 'line renders';\n      write(file, `it('${title}', () => {});\\n`);\n      const matrix = [{\n        id: 'F1', statement, appliesTo: ['line'],\n        notApplicable: Object.fromEntries(CHART_TYPES.filter(type => type !== 'line').map(type => [type, 'Only a line fixture.'])),\n        evidence: { line: [{ kind: 'unit', file, title }] },\n      }];\n      write('acceptance/matrix.json', JSON.stringify(matrix));\n      const git = (...args: string[]) => execFileSync('git', args, { cwd: root, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'inherit'] });\n      git('init', '-q');\n      git('add', '.');\n      git('-c', 'user.name=Fixture', '-c', 'user.email=fixture@example.test', '-c', 'commit.gpgsign=false', 'commit', '-qm', 'Fixture');\n\n      const relative = defaultResultFile('unit');\n      const result = write(relative, JSON.stringify({\n        testResults: [{ name: file, assertionResults: [{ title, status: 'passed', ancestorTitles: [] }] }],\n      }));\n      const recorded = { ...snapshot(root, citedTestFiles(matrix)), resultSha256: hashFile(result) };\n      write(relative.replace(/\\.json$/, '.provenance.json'), JSON.stringify(recorded));\n      const direct = check({ root, release: true, resultFiles: [result] });\n      expect(direct.exitCode).toBe(0);\n      expect(direct.rows[0]!.cells.line.status).toBe('pass');\n\n      await stageSite(path.join(root, 'apps/docs/dist'), async tmp => {\n        fs.mkdirSync(path.join(tmp, 'assets'), { recursive: true });\n        fs.writeFileSync(path.join(tmp, 'assets/site.css'), 'body {}\\n');\n        const { checker } = await readConformance({ root });\n        expect(checker.refused).toBeNull();\n        expect(checker.files).toMatchObject([{ file: relative, counted: true, why: null }]);\n        expect(checker.rows.get('F1')!.cells.line!.status).toBe(direct.rows[0]!.cells.line.status);\n\n        fs.appendFileSync(specFile, '\\nA source edit made after recording.\\n');\n        const stale = await readConformance({ root });\n        expect(stale.checker.files).toMatchObject([{ file: relative, counted: false, why: 'provenance does not match the working tree' }]);\n        expect(stale.criteria[0]!.verdict).toEqual([{ id: 'F1', text: 'not recorded for this revision' }]);\n      });\n    } finally {\n      fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  it('a size record of another pack is not recorded for this revision, and no engine\\'s', async () => {\n    // As the checker's own test of size records builds it (acceptance/test/check.test.mjs, defect 5).\n    const dir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(cacheDir, 'conformance-'));\n    try {\n      fs.mkdirSync(path.join(dir, 'docs'));\n      fs.copyFileSync(path.join(fixtures, 'docs/02-product-spec.md'), path.join(dir, 'docs/02-product-spec.md'));\n      const matrix = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(fixtures, 'matrix.json'), 'utf8')).map((row: object) => ({ ...row, evidence: {}, weak: {} }));\n      matrix[0].evidence = { line: [{ kind: 'size', file: 'size.json', entries: ['line only'] }] };\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, 'matrix.json'), JSON.stringify(matrix));\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, 'size.json'), JSON.stringify({ packed: { axylo: 'sha512-measured' }, rows: [{ entry: 'line only', minBytes: 2000, totalGzipBytes: 1000, targetKiB: 1 }] }));\n      const options = { root: dir, matrixFile: path.join(dir, 'matrix.json'), resultFiles: [], sizeTargets: { 'line only': 1 } };\n      const same = await readChecker({ ...options, packIntegrity: 'sha512-measured' });\n      expect(same.rows.get('F1')!.cells.line!.status).toBe('pass');\n      const other = await readChecker({ ...options, packIntegrity: 'sha512-current' });\n      const line = other.rows.get('F1')!.cells.line!;\n      expect(line.status).toBe('not recorded for this revision');\n      expect(line.reports).toEqual([{ file: 'size.json', source: 'size', results: ['not recorded'], engine: null, counted: false, why: 'the size record measured another pack (sha512-measured)', commit: null }]);\n      expect(evidenceFor([{ id: 'F1', criterion: '' }], other)).toEqual({\n        verdict: [{ id: 'F1', text: 'not recorded for this revision' }],\n        engines: { chromium: 'not recorded', firefox: 'not recorded', webkit: 'not recorded', null: 'not recorded' },\n      });\n    } finally {\n      fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    }\n  });\n\n  it('a refused matrix leaves every criterion not recorded', async () => {\n    const checker = await readChecker({ root: fixtures, matrixFile: path.join(fixtures, 'stale.json'), resultFiles: [path.join(fixtures, 'results.json')] });\n    expect(checker.refused!.join('\\n')).toMatch(/stale criterion ID: F88/);\n    expect(evidenceFor([{ id: 'F1', criterion: '' }], checker)).toEqual({\n      verdict: [{ id: 'F1', text: 'not recorded' }],\n      engines: { chromium: 'not recorded', firefox: 'not recorded', webkit: 'not recorded', null: 'not recorded' },\n    });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('what is counted', () => {\n  // A checker report as readChecker returns it, written out: one row, two engines, one stale run.\n  const report = (file: string, engine: string, results: string[], counted = true, commit = 'aaaaaaa1') => ({ file, source: 'run', results, engine, counted, commit });\n  const checker = {\n    refused: null,\n    rows: new Map([['I4', { statement: '', cells: {\n      line: { status: 'pass', reports: [report('browser.json', 'chromium', ['pass']), report('browser-webkit.json', 'webkit', ['fail', 'pass'])] },\n      donut: { status: 'not applicable', reports: [] },\n    } }]]),\n  };\n\n  it('each engine says what its own results said, and the verdict lists the chart types', () => {\n    expect(evidenceFor([{ id: 'I4', criterion: '' }], checker)).toEqual({\n      verdict: [{ id: 'I4', text: 'pass (line); not applicable (donut)' }],\n      engines: { chromium: 'pass', firefox: 'not recorded', webkit: 'fail/pass', null: 'not recorded' },\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('a row with a result from another revision has no verdict for this one', () => {\n    const stale = { ...checker, rows: new Map([['I4', { statement: '', cells: { line: { status: 'pass', reports: [report('browser-firefox.json', 'firefox', ['pass'], false, 'bbbbbbb2')] } } }]]) };\n    expect(evidenceFor([{ id: 'I4', criterion: '' }], stale)).toEqual({\n      verdict: [{ id: 'I4', text: 'not recorded for this revision' }],\n      engines: { chromium: 'not recorded', firefox: 'not recorded for this revision (results from bbbbbbb)', webkit: 'not recorded', null: 'not recorded' },\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('a row the checker does not have is not recorded', () => {\n    expect(evidenceFor([{ id: 'A99', criterion: '' }], checker).verdict).toEqual([{ id: 'A99', text: 'not recorded' }]);\n  });\n});\n# Conformance table\n\nAfter this page you know which WCAG 2.2 success criteria the specification cites, what Axylo does for each, what evidence was recorded for them when this site was built, why no test covers the other level A and AA criteria, and what that evidence cannot show.\n\nThis page is generated each time the site is built, from the specification's criterion rows and from the report of the acceptance checker. It says only what they record; where they record nothing, it says \"not recorded\". It is not a claim that a page using Axylo conforms: conformance belongs to a whole page, and the page is yours.\n\n## What the evidence can and cannot show\n\nOn release candidate `1e93128`, Codex CLI `gpt-6.2-sol` and Claude Code `claude-opus-5-5` each passed three uncoached attempts on each of four fixed line and bar tasks. All 24 attempts passed after the transcript re-audit. In Chrome 158, each saved answer passed the reader checks without error diagnostics on both inputs in the Los Angeles and Tokyo time zones. This agent rehearsal gives no estimate of general success and provides no evidence of human or screen-reader usability or WCAG conformance. The prompt restricted agents to the published docs for guidance, and the audit checked recorded access. The filesystem did not enforce docs-only access.\n\n- **Automated checks only.** The acceptance tests check structure: names, roles, focus order, contrast, sizes and text. They do not show that a person using a screen reader understands a chart.\n- **No screen-reader rehearsal was done for 1.0.** No screen reader has been run against these charts, so nothing in this documentation says what a screen reader speaks.\n- **No usability testing with disabled people.** Axylo is built by one person with no access to study participants, and no claim of usability testing with disabled users is made.\n- **Engines, not browsers.** Browser results are recorded per engine: Chrome, and Firefox and WebKit as built by Playwright. WebKit results are Playwright's WebKit, not Safari. Nothing has been run on a phone.\n- **Right-to-left pages.** Right-to-left text renders, but the chart's layout is not mirrored.\n- **Transformed ancestors.** A chart inside a translated or scaled element is exact. Inside a rotated, skewed or mirrored element it draws, but pointing and tooltip placement are wrong; that is not supported in 1.0.\n\n## What you must supply\n\nAxylo can only describe what it is given. A chart needs a meaningful name (`title`, or `labelledBy` pointing at your heading), series names, units on value fields, and the page's own structure around it. A compact chart fed by `append` has no Pause control, since it has no toolbar: a page that streams into compact tiles must give the reader its own way to pause them (WCAG 2.2.2). [Accessibility](accessibility.md#what-you-must-supply) has the details.\n\n## The criteria the specification cites\n\n[table: conformance](../../../acceptance/check.mjs)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
