19320, 76 cited test hashes in the sidecar · provenance does not match the working tree\n\n## Packed size measurement\n\nMeasured from the pack this tree makes (sha512-H9mJWNoPledc…, commit 91d12bf).\n\n- line only (examples/first-chart/npm.ts) · 281,514 minified JS bytes, 96.32 KiB gzipped, 98 KiB target · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n- everything (export * from axylo) · 335,598 minified JS bytes, 115.48 KiB gzipped, 116 KiB target · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n| P6 | Download: exact minified and gzipped bytes, CSS included, within the DX7 targets (116 KiB everything, 98 KiB line only). | pass (size-latest.json pass) | pass (size-latest.json pass) | pass (size-latest.json pass) | pass (size-latest.json pass) | pass (size-latest.json pass) | pass (size-latest.json pass) |\n| P7 | Memory, measured after forced collection: bytes owned by Axylo beyond the caller's columns for 1,000,000 points at most 1.1 × the caller's two columns (owner, 2026-11-18), and no upward heap slope over 1,000 create–destroy cycles (provisional). | not run (unit.json not recorded, browser.json not recorded) | not run | not run | not run | not run | not run |\n| P8 | 40 compact charts created on one page, each 160 × 48 px with one series: total main-thread task time, median of 20 runs, at most 80 ms (provisional). | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not run |\n\n## What stands between this tree and a release\n\n### Failing cells\n\nNo failing cells recorded.\n\n### Released with documented gaps\n\n- **I6** · compact · A compact chart fed by append shows no Pause/Resume control (spec 3.7: no toolbar), so the chart does not meet I6 itself: the documentation hands pausing to the author (WCAG 2.2.2). No test checks a page that pauses streaming compact tiles.\n- **DX12** · line, bar · An external run recorded the accepted agent rehearsal for 1e93128. The rehearsal must be repeated on the release commit. The record covers two models, four fixed line and bar tasks, two inputs per task and two time zones in Chrome 158. The graded inputs missed decimal grammar errors found in a separate probe. One attempt's eligibility changed after the run, and docs-only access was not enforced by the filesystem. General agent success, model rankings, human and screen-reader usability, and WCAG conformance remain unestablished.\n  - area, scatter, donut, compact · An external run recorded the accepted agent rehearsal for 1e93128. The rehearsal must be repeated on the release commit. The record covers two models, four fixed line and bar tasks, two inputs per task and two time zones in Chrome 158. Area, scatter, donut and compact charts were outside those tasks. The graded inputs missed decimal grammar errors found in a separate probe. One attempt's eligibility changed after the run, and docs-only access was not enforced by the filesystem. General agent success, model rankings, human and screen-reader usability, and WCAG conformance remain unestablished.\n\n### Weak cells\n\n- **L1** · Weak · line · Generated label sets are checked only in Node, against the layout with a fixed-width test measurer, not as painted text in a browser. The 200 % condition doubles the page's inherited font size; the browser's own text-only zoom is not run. The late font is checked at 480 and 1,280 px only, without text spacing or the 200 % condition. No line chart with an unordered category x is drawn in these tests, so middle truncation, the full text in tooltip and table, and the hidden-labels note with AX143 are not exercised on this type.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
